==========================================
DAY 27 NOTES — Basic Linux Hardening Checklist
Date: 25-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- Hardening = many small consistent checks, not one big fix
- Today's checklist combines: SUID check (Day 8), world-writable files (Day 2),
  sudo access review (Day 3), SSH config (Day 18-19), firewall status (Day 21),
  pending updates (Day 9), failed login count (Day 7)
- PermitRootLogin should be 'no' regardless of password strength — reduces attack surface
- Disable PasswordAuthentication ONLY after confirming SSH key login works (avoid lockout!)
- A clean check today doesn't guarantee clean tomorrow — hardening is a ROUTINE

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] find -perm -4000 (SUID check)
[ ] find -perm -002 (world-writable check)
[ ] getent group sudo (sudo access review)
[ ] grep on sshd_config (SSH hardening check)
[ ] ufw status verbose (firewall check)
[ ] apt list --upgradable (patch check)

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ find / -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null
> 

$ getent group sudo
> 

$ sudo ufw status verbose
> 


